course: dictionary
lesson: 15023
title: A welcome respite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A respite is a short rest or break from something hard, painful or unpleasant. It is a noun, so you can write a respite or some respites. «After hours of heavy rain, the hikers finally got a respite when the sun came out.» The rain was the hard thing, and the sun gave them a break from it.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like «from» and «without» often sit near it. «The baby cried all night, and the family had no respite.» No respite means there was no break at all. To check your meaning, swap in "short break" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Respite is also used in family life. Respite care is when someone else looks after a person who is ill or disabled, so their carer can rest. «Every Tuesday, a helper comes so that Dad can have a respite.» The break is for the carer, not for the person being cared for.
fact: A respite is a short break or rest.
fact: «A brief respite» means a short rest.
fact: «Without respite» means without any break at all.
fact: Respite care is a short break for a carer, when someone else takes over.
fact: In old law, respite can also mean a delay before a punishment.
exercise: «The rain stopped for a short respite, and we ran to the park.» What is a respite here? | *A short break from the rain | A large puddle | A type of umbrella | A long, wet walk
exercise: «The workers had no respite from the loud drilling all day.» What does no respite mean? | A new drill for the workers | *No break at all from the noise | Loud music at a party | No noise at all
exercise: Which phrase means a short break for a carer who looks after someone who is ill? | Bedtime story | Heavy lifting | Careful driving | *Respite care
test: «Sam took a brief respite before the next lesson.» What is a brief respite? | A long holiday | *A short rest | A school trip | A test
test: Which word is closest in meaning to respite? | Danger | Speed | *Break | Noise
exam: Which sentence uses respite correctly? | We played respite on the football pitch. | The cake had a respite in the oven. | Respite is a colour of the sky. | *The soldiers had a short respite from the fighting.
